  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Coal Gasification Project, through Government of Turkey</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $437,020 grant supported a feasibility study examining technical and economic aspects of a proposed pilot plant that would convert coal into substitute natural gas, which would then be introduced into Turkey&apos;s gas transmission system. This plant would use existing coal resources to create a new energy source which would have a net lower environmental impact than combustion of the same coal for power production. The grantee was Turkiye Komur Isletmeleri Kurumu, a state-owned mining company in Turkey.</narrative>
  </description>
